Z||000006||Cooter||08-04-2001||10:10 PM||||One thing that I don't understand- Why prime the mouldings, park lights and other stuff that is next to impossible to sand? The edges around all the mouldings are a pain to make paint stick, so I hope you sanded the fool out of it before squirting the peanut butter  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rob Durham||08-04-2001||10:42 PM||||The trim pieces are epoxied in place, sanded well and the small gaps filled in to make it look like part of the body. <P>The marker lights are going away I was too tired at 4:30 this morning to do any more work.<P>Semproducts (http://www.semproducts.com) makes some killer adhesives and fillers for plastic and FRP parts.<P>I know my posts are low (one reason for not posting much is because of the arrogance of others) but I do know what I’m doing, I have been working with fiberglass and plastics since the early 80’s, I owned a kit car company called Italian Image from 1987 to1993 until Ferrari shut us down, I have been painting and restoring cars since 1980, I do all my mold work, prototyping, painting, metal work ect.<P>I just thought I would share what I did yesterday with you guys.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://rs-designs.com/87GT.html" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://rs-designs.com/Banner.jpg">  </A>||||reg||11
Z||000008||Sage||08-04-2001||11:57 PM||||Looks good to me...very good.  Are the rear quarters ones that you made, or the originals reworked?<P>  I'm right with ya on the post frequency, and the reason.  Hope you will post more pics as things progress, as I would like to see the finished product!  As for your ability, the pics speak volumes.<P>Have a good one!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rob Durham||08-05-2001||09:52 AM||||Thanks Sage,<P>I just reworked the original quarters then glassed the entire lower quarter<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://rs-designs.com/87GT.html" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://rs-designs.com/Banner.jpg">  </A>||||reg||1
