Z||000016||Jay||08-05-2001||12:24 PM||||Rob I really like those side vents.  I'm not a big fan of the ones that stick out, kinda looks too aftermarket for my taste.  Do you have molds for those and are you selling them?  I'd be interested in a set of them.  Hook me up with an e-mail jaygrande@home.com<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Rob Durham||08-05-2001||02:24 PM||||Sorry Jay, no  molds just drew the opening on the car and cut, with Aus body package coming out I didn't think there would be much interest I just don't like waiting for things.<P>After sanding the sh!t out of the trim I used an epoxy adhesive to bond it back to the car and to fill the gap above and below it, then I sprayed a coat of epoxy primer before using the filler primer.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://rs-designs.com/87GT.html" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://rs-designs.com/Banner.jpg">   </A><p>[This message has been edited by Rob Durham (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
